          </figure>

          <div class="mechanisms">
            <div class="mechanism"><span class="index">01</span><h3>French-specific depth</h3><p>A French-only service can connect pronunciation, grammar, cultural pragmatics, TEF/TCF-oriented needs, CEFR, and Canadian CLB/NCLC goals more tightly than a broad multilingual catalogue.<a class="cite" href="#ref-17">17</a><a class="cite" href="#ref-18">18</a></p></div>
            <div class="mechanism"><span class="index">02</span><h3>Four-skill continuity</h3><p>Speaking, listening, reading, and writing should reuse the same language targets. This makes transfer a designed property of the pathway rather than a separate add-on.</p></div>
            <div class="mechanism"><span class="index">03</span><h3>Human + AI + environment</h3><p>AI can supply frequency and immediacy; humans supply judgment, empathy, pragmatics, and accountability; immersive environments supply context and action. Each compensates for limits in the others.</p></div>
            <div class="mechanism"><span class="index">04</span><h3>Lifespan adaptation</h3><p>The same curriculum spine can be expressed through guardian-supported play, adolescent autonomy, adult goals, or seated older-adult sessions rather than forcing one interface and tone on everyone.</p></div>
          </div>

